                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "846610fc-686f-31f1-b435-a0535d2b0d1b",
                        "entry_id": "006c2780-ece2-3dff-937d-897cad8688f1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сравнительно молодая наука на стыке биологии и химии о химическом составе живых клеток и организмов и о лежащих в основе их жизнедеятельности химических процессах"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb135d7b-d09b-4a63-a1f3-29d1b975dccb",
                                "sense_id": "846610fc-686f-31f1-b435-a0535d2b0d1b",
                                "text": "Современная биохимия начала активно использовать соединения рутения — ближайшего аналога железа для выявления биологической роли оксида азота (М) [32]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc9344cd-c929-385e-81aa-45835a5dca51",
                        "entry_id": "006c2780-ece2-3dff-937d-897cad8688f1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "химические процессы, характерные для того или иного рода живой материи, как предмет изучения данной научной дисциплины"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5211ee31-44f2-4414-8a8b-706275f4bbc6",
                                "sense_id": "bc9344cd-c929-385e-81aa-45835a5dca51",
                                "text": "Биохимия человека такова, что требует постоянной алертности мозга на одну пятую часть его мощности, а это поддерживается лишь уровнем кетостеронов — гормонов пола в крови."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d9d019b-8bd9-4acd-aa86-856675d0ef4f",
                        "source_entry_id": "006c2780-ece2-3dff-937d-897cad8688f1",
                        "target_lang_word": "biochemistry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "biochemistry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "863b72ec-2aab-3988-81a6-b04d3a9961c3",
                                        "entry_id": "af9ece19-d1db-353c-bcfd-8d197c1a7a19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The chemistry of those compounds that occur in living organisms, and the processes that occur in their metabolism and catabolism; the study of such chemistry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d17476c2-7c69-488d-bb68-9243603dd535",
                                                "sense_id": "863b72ec-2aab-3988-81a6-b04d3a9961c3",
                                                "text": "My aunt has a degree in biochemistry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5af2c23c-33af-38c4-988b-8039bba791f0",
                                        "entry_id": "af9ece19-d1db-353c-bcfd-8d197c1a7a19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The chemical characteristics of a particular living organism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f1d9ec2-ebf2-4f0c-bc4f-67b6c0b87b8e",
                                                "sense_id": "5af2c23c-33af-38c4-988b-8039bba791f0",
                                                "text": "The biochemistries of fungal and bacterial cells are quite distinct."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f4476e1-ab1d-4c15-a072-afbce95518fd",
                                                "sense_id": "5af2c23c-33af-38c4-988b-8039bba791f0",
                                                "text": "They [viruses] use more varied biochemistry than cellular life, storing their genetic information as both single- and double-stranded DNA as well as RNA."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b795164-ffa8-38f2-8af6-636f85d164ee",
                                        "entry_id": "af9ece19-d1db-353c-bcfd-8d197c1a7a19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The biochemical activity associated with a particular chemical or condition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "796f0344-0e3b-4f91-a099-2c27fd8de0eb",
                                                "sense_id": "4b795164-ffa8-38f2-8af6-636f85d164ee",
                                                "text": "Our study compared the biochemistries of epilepsy and Parkinson's."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09c60aea-d087-4215-adfc-064cbbb88f00",
                                                "sense_id": "4b795164-ffa8-38f2-8af6-636f85d164ee",
                                                "text": "The biochemistry of NO differs from that of NO₂."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
